# DERIVED, not vendored-and-committed. `vendor/ffmpeg.pin` (a URL and a sha256) is the thing under
# version control; `vendor/fetch.sh` turns it into these. The extracted tree is 100 MB across
# 8,540 files, which would dominate the repository and make `git log` over it unreadable, and it
# is reproducible from the pin by construction.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING TO IT: if you ever decide to commit the tree instead -- which is a
# legitimate choice for a network-free build environment -- these two lines are what you delete.
# Do not add a broader pattern here; an over-eager ignore is how a vendored dependency goes
# missing from a clone and the failure shows up as a build error nobody can reproduce.
/vendor/ffmpeg-*/
/vendor/*.tar.xz
